{
  "__schema__": "Authoritative weapon-damage overrides for monsters whose source-data averages are wrong/ambiguous (multi-component riders, data typos, condition-only attacks). Keyed by monster name -> attack-slot index (string '0'..'3') -> spec. Spec fields: 'name' (book attack name, reference only), 'damage' (list of {type, num_dice, die_size} dice groups; the ability modifier is NOT included here), 'mod' (the book +M ability modifier; the converter sets bonus_damage = mod - engine_auto_mod so the total lands on dice+mod regardless of buggy source PB), 'condition_only' (true => no damage roll, but the attack still lands its conditions). On-hit riders: 'conditions' (list of {condition_name, condition_duration?, escape_dc?, contested?} applied on a hit; 'Poisoned' uses the active-condition system, 'Grappled' routes through the shared grapple core — escape_dc overrides the computed 10+STR+prof, contested=true rolls Athletics instead of auto-applying), and 'mastery' (a WeaponMastery name; 'Topple' is how on-hit Prone is modelled — the bestiary auto-enables weapon_mastery for the monster). The converter (Monster.to_weapons) consults this before falling back to average-reconstruction.",
